outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014hZWugFvcBrpUNba8E1RLR", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 377936, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014hZWugFvcBrpUNba8E1RLR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 382593, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (round halves up), even though its own docstring says banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That's why `test_half_even` failed: `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986), I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe advisory system had no record of FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement against it. The fix is based only on the test and the docstring, which agree with each other. I didn't merge the PR because it still needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01THJzHMVMZQzhEv1YMiZMQD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FweDLeNL2tuBRQzDH1A1vg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014uj7Z9W7DLYAuC7XdmMnTK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Gh6GeaFza1rYfsAHQ6DJUY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Egej2hmooXb3zXTeoEeB61", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KRhStBkBXcqrbLBsySePRw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01J2yL3FgDFauWcCsp2xqftq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014hZWugFvcBrpUNba8E1RLR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring said ROUND_HALF_EVEN.\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (round halves up), even though its own docstring says banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That's why `test_half_even` failed: `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986), I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe advisory system had no record of FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement against it. The fix is based only on the test and the docstring, which agree with each other. I didn't merge the PR because it still needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}